11. Idempotency in ms.
Idempotency ensures that repeated execution of the same request produces the same result without unintended side effects. This is crucial in microservices, 
especially in scenarios where requests might be replayed, retried, or duplicated due to network failures or system errors.

Why Is Idempotency Important?
✅ Prevents duplicate operations (e.g., multiple payments for the same order). ✅ Ensures consistency across distributed systems. ✅ Improves fault tolerance by allowing safe retries.
